v run pytest -q`, `uv run ruff check .`) passes.\n\n## Functional requirements\n\n- **R-1** The module `app_int.main` (file `src/app_int/main.py`) defines a public function named `square`.\n- **R-2** `square` takes exactly one positional argument, `n`.\n- **R-3** For an integer input `n`, `square(n)` returns the integer `n * n`.\n- **R-4** `square` returns the correct, non-negative result for negative integers (for example, `square(-3) == 9`).\n- **R-5** `square(0)` returns `0`.\n- **R-6** `square` has a docstring that describes what it returns. This matches the existing functions in the module.\n- **R-7** `square` has type annotations for its parameter and return value. This matches the existing functions in the module.\n- **R-8** The test suite under `tests/` has at least one test that imports `square` from `app_int.main` and checks its result for at least one positive integer, one negative integer, and zero.\n\n## Non-functional requirements\n\n- **R-9** The existing public functions `health_check` and `add` keep their behaviour, and their existing tests still pass.\n- **R-10** `uv run pytest -q` exits with status 0.\n- **R-11** `uv run ruff check .` exits with status 0.\n- **R-12** No new runtime dependencies are added to `pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Assumptions (inferred, not stated in the task)\n\n- **A-1** The task's path \"app_int/main.py\" means `src/app_int/main.py`. That is the repository's only `app_int/main.py`.\n- **A-2** The function's contract covers integers (`int -> int`), matching the style of `add(a: int, b: int) -> int`. Behaviour for floats, bools or other numeric types is not part of the contract and is not tested.\n- **A-3** Input validation (for example, raising `TypeError` on non-numeric input) is not required.\n- **A-4** \"With a test\" means one or more pytest tests. Adding them to the existing `tests/test_main.py` is acceptable.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Other math helpers (cube, power, square root, and so on).\n- A CLI, API endpoint or any other interface that exposes `square`.\n- Changes to the README, CI workflows or Dark Factory configuration.\n- Refactoring the existing functions.\n\n## Open questions\n\nNone of these block the work; each one is covered by an assumption above.\n\n## Possible follow-ups (not requirements)\n\n- Decide whether `square` should accept floats or other numeric types (see A-2).\nEOF\ncat > $D/acceptance_criteria.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"description\": \"(R-1) `from app_int.main import square` succeeds, and `square` is a callable defined in src/app_int/main.py.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"description\": \"(R-2) `inspect.signature(square)` has exactly one parameter, named `n`.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"description\": \"(R-3) square(3) == 9, square(1) == 1, and square(12) == 144, and each result is an int.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"description\": \"(R-4) square(-3) == 9 and square(-1) == 1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"description\": \"(R-5) square(0) == 0.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"description\": \"(R-6) `square.__doc__` is a non-empty string.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"description\": \"(R-7) `square.__annotations__` contains an entry for 'n' and an entry for 'return'.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"description\": \"(R-8) At least one test function under tests/ imports `square` from `app_int.main` and asserts its result for a positive integer, a negative integer, and zero.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-9\", \"description\": \"(R-9) The existing tests test_health_check_reports_ok and test_add_returns_the_sum are still present and pass, and health_check() == {'status': 'ok'} and add(2, 3) == 5.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-10\", \"description\": \"(R-10) `uv run pytest -q` exits with status 0.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-11\", \"description\": \"(R-11) `uv run ruff check .` exits with status 0.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-12\", \"description\": \"(R-12) The `dependencies` list in the [project] section of pyproject.toml is unchanged (still empty).\"}\n  ]\n}\nEOF\npython3 -m json.tool $D/acceptance_criteria.json >/dev/null && echo ok; git status --porcelain","description":"Write BA artifacts and validate JSON"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the requirements and acceptance criteria for adding `square(n)` with a test. I couldn't run a JSON or schema check because shell access was denied; I wrote `acceptance_criteria.json` by hand to match the schema (a `criteria` list of `id` and `description` objects, nothing else).\n\n**Goal:** `app_int.main` gets a public `square(n)` that returns `n * n`, plus a test, and both quality-gate commands (`pytest` and `ruff`) still pass.\n\n**`requirements.md`** has 12 numbered requirements:\n- **What the function does (R-1 to R-7):** it is defined in `src/app_int/main.py` and takes one argument, `n`. It returns `n * n` for integers, including negatives and zero. It has a docstring and type hints, like the existing functions.\n- **The test (R-8):** it must check a positive number, a negative number and zero.\n- **Other checks (R-9 to R-12):** `health_check` and `add` behave as before and their tests still pass. `uv run pytest -q` and `uv run ruff check .` both exit 0. No new runtime dependencies are added.\n\n**`acceptance_criteria.json`** has 12 pass/fail checks, AC-1 to AC-12. Each one maps to the requirement with the same number and names a concrete check, such as `square(-3) == 9` or an exit status of 0.\n\n**Assumptions I made rather than ask about:**\n- The task says `app_int/main.py`; I took that to mean `src/app_int/main.py`, the only file with that name.\n- The function only has to handle integers (`int -> int`), like `add`.\n- It doesn't need to reject bad input.\n- The test can go in the existing `tests/test_main.py`.\n\n**Out of scope:** other maths helpers, any CLI or API, and changes to the docs or CI. Supporting floats is listed as a possible follow-up.\n\nNo questions block the work, and I didn't change any repository source files.\n\nFiles are in `.dark-factory/runs/e5c7dd5c-8fdf-4c4d-a11c-894790000709/artifacts/BA/`:\n- `requirements.md`\n- `acceptance_criteria.json`","ttft_ms":2118,"type":"result","duration_ms":40402,"uuid":"1e7091a6-c41c-4877-8c7e-e715e7552b85","ttft_stream_ms":1776,"time_to_request_ms":171,"first_content_frame_ms":1776,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
